To run the main algorithm run file GT.m, this shows the proccess frame-by-frame and creates results.txt with the data from the algorithm.(Goals: 1,2,3,4)

Goal 5: running staticHeatmap.m creates static_heatmap.fig and shows the trajectory heatmap of the pedestrians, running dynamicHeatmap.m runs the same algorithm but incrementaly

Goal 6: running EM.m displays and saves to the following files (BIC_CURVE.fig, CLUSTER_MEANS.fig, CLUSTER_SHAPES.fig and CONFIDENCE.fig) where you can most importantly observe the shape of each cluster of trajectories and the phisical shape they have on the image. Statistics about each cluster can be observed in the terminal or the file cluster_statistics.txt
In the current iteration, trajectories in Cluster 1 a longer duration and length but shorter net-displacement than ones in Cluster 2, meaning trajecotries in cluster 2 are more efficient and direct while the ones in cluster 1 are more winding.

Goal 7: running performance.m creates the folder "evaluation_output" and its contents:
    success_plot.png: shows the Success rate in relation with the IoU.
    fp_fn_summary.png: shows the stats related to an IoU threshold of 0.5
    fp_fn_per_frame_.png: shows the number of flase positives and false negatives per frame for the duration of the video with an IoU threshold of 0.5
    evaluation_summary.txt: shows the stats for the run with IoU threshold of 0.5
    error_frame_0016.png: shows an example of a false positive, where the pedestrian is already in frame but the ground truth hasn't taken them into account
    error_frame_0022.png: shows an example of a false negative, whre the pedestrian is behind an obstacle and our algorithm can't detect him

Goal 8: 
    running ai.py creates the NNresults.txt by running the model named "yolo26n.pt" over the video.
    running NNperformance.m creates the folder "NNevaluation_output" and its contents, similar to Goal 7 but using the NN instead of our algorithm.
    The NN has better performance than our algorithm in all metrics
    The Scuccess rate over IoU threshold ratio is always better than our algorithm 
    at IoU threshold of 0.5 it has relatively:
    ~8% better Precision
    ~28% better Recall
    ~18% better F1-score